1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,979
Look with your heart and truly see

2
00:00:32,979 --> 00:00:35,960
The truth is not far away

3
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:38,980
Hey you good or bad, true or false

4
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:41,980
You can't escape the gray smoke in your soul

5
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:44,960
Take all your courage

6
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,140
Maybe then you can save the world

7
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,299
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

8
00:00:50,299 --> 00:00:53,719
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:56,679
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

10
00:00:56,679 --> 00:00:57,900
Mojo Spy

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Following the clues, the heroes finally find the Illumin-Eye's hideout—Tuna Supermarket

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Lord Eye triggers a mechanism and turns the supermarket into a giant warship

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The Illumin-Eye members each hold a treasure, ready for the final showdown

14
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,000
Supermarket Brawl

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,659
What is this place?

16
00:01:41,659 --> 00:01:45,200
I think the Illumin-Eye, just as the Illumin Doctrine records,

17
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,840
has turned the supermarket into something else

18
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,960
to complete the final ritual

19
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,939
The final ritual?

20
00:01:50,939 --> 00:01:52,900
What happens when it's done?

21
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:55,200
I'm sure nothing good will come of it

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,799
The Illumin-Eye's altar is up above

23
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,879
We have to hurry and catch up

24
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,479
Officers

25
00:02:16,479 --> 00:02:17,680
How have you been?

26
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,560
Dorothy!

27
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:22,719
Today your evil cult falls!

28
00:02:22,719 --> 00:02:24,639
So just surrender already!

29
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:28,719
Then let's see what you've got!

30
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:38,360
Officer Han!

31
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,639
Captain Han!

32
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:41,419
Are you all right?

33
00:02:41,419 --> 00:02:42,259
Where are you?

34
00:02:42,259 --> 00:02:48,000
Stop it!

35
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,159
It's no use!

36
00:02:49,159 --> 00:02:51,780
You'll be in the next world soon,

37
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,939
blown apart like flower petals,

38
00:02:53,939 --> 00:02:55,759
reuniting with the beautiful Captain Han!

39
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:57,639
Prepare to die!

40
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:03,360
You!

41
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:05,700
Dorothy!

42
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:08,260
Still won't surrender?

43
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:10,560
Captain Han, are you all right?

44
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,720
You're okay. Thank goodness!

45
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,580
Just a cheap trick!

46
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:16,980
But it was enough to take him out!

47
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,300
You're surrounded!

48
00:03:24,379 --> 00:03:25,379
Hey!

49
00:03:35,379 --> 00:03:36,379
Anyone here?

50
00:03:45,379 --> 00:03:47,379
Strange—where did everyone go?

51
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:57,479
Kid

52
00:03:57,479 --> 00:04:00,859
Eating too much candy gives you cavities, you know.

53
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,219
Mr. k!

54
00:04:09,219 --> 00:04:12,519
Kid, wandering around the supermarket all alone is dangerous.

55
00:04:12,519 --> 00:04:14,900
How about Uncle sends you back home?

56
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:17,819
Take a look at my magnifying glass!

57
00:04:31,699 --> 00:04:31,759
You can't escape.

58
00:04:31,759 --> 00:04:35,899
I'm such an idiot.

59
00:04:35,899 --> 00:04:43,879
Jingjing

60
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:45,899
Stop hiding.

61
00:04:45,899 --> 00:04:47,600
I can already see you.

62
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,980
Come out now.

63
00:05:12,399 --> 00:05:13,060
Jingjing, stop hiding.

64
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,459
I can already see you.

65
00:05:14,459 --> 00:05:17,579
Jingjing? Ah.

66
00:05:17,579 --> 00:05:20,180
If you don't come out, it'll be such a pity.

67
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:23,159
Because I've got something great here.

68
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:26,040
It's a giant limited-edition poster of Miss MU!

69
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:30,520
No choice then.

70
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:34,580
Looks like I have to use this on you.

71
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,500
You cute little bad dog.

72
00:05:50,639 --> 00:05:53,439
Go find the kid playing hide-and-seek.

73
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:54,819
Over there.

74
00:05:54,819 --> 00:05:56,939
Remember to be polite.

75
00:06:12,899 --> 00:06:13,019
Slow down.

76
00:06:13,019 --> 00:06:14,060
Wait for me!

77
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:58,959
Hawxing!

78
00:06:58,959 --> 00:07:01,479
Fighting the Illumin-Eye

79
00:07:01,479 --> 00:07:02,599
won't end well.

80
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,579
This is my final

81
00:07:11,579 --> 00:07:12,339
word of advice.

82
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,639
Hawxing.

83
00:07:33,639 --> 00:07:36,279
You once saved my life,

84
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:37,839
so I've tried to talk some sense into you.

85
00:07:37,839 --> 00:07:39,919
Why do you insist on opposing us?

86
00:07:39,919 --> 00:07:42,919
The Illumin-Eye claims to understand love and ideals,

87
00:07:42,919 --> 00:07:44,319
yet he keeps doing evil,

88
00:07:44,319 --> 00:07:45,339
bringing people pain.

89
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,659
I'm curious

90
00:07:46,659 --> 00:07:48,379
what kind of love and ideals

91
00:07:48,379 --> 00:07:50,420
drive him to do such contradictory things.

92
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:53,040
I'll make him tell the truth.

93
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,019
He understands love and ideals?

94
00:08:01,019 --> 00:08:04,259
The reason I joined this ridiculous organization

95
00:08:04,259 --> 00:08:06,379
is that I was crazy about Dorothy.

96
00:08:06,379 --> 00:08:08,740
Even though she never gave me a second glance,

97
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:10,980
I still won't give up.

98
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,379
I thought

99
00:08:12,379 --> 00:08:14,319
that as long as I stayed by her side,

100
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:15,339
caring for her, protecting her...

101
00:08:15,339 --> 00:08:16,719
Pass love on to him.

102
00:08:16,719 --> 00:08:17,759
One day,

103
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:19,839
he’ll learn to treasure my feelings.

104
00:08:19,839 --> 00:08:21,620
But, gradually,

105
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:23,099
I discovered I was wrong.

106
00:08:23,099 --> 00:08:24,939
It turned out he never understood what love is.

107
00:08:24,939 --> 00:08:26,180
He would only foolishly swoon over

108
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:27,420
flashy, hollow things.

109
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:30,099
For years, he hadn’t changed one bit.

110
00:08:30,099 --> 00:08:31,980
Lord Eye exploited exactly that

111
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:33,700
to make him serve heart and soul.

112
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,340
The love and dreams they keep preaching

113
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:37,539
are only self-deception

114
00:08:37,539 --> 00:08:39,319
and nonsense to fool people.

115
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:41,240
Deep down,

116
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,500
they only think selfishly—

117
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,340
about themselves.

118
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:46,580
My only regret is that I fell too deep for Dorothy.

119
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,900
There’s no turning back now.

120
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,620
Maybe this is what love is.

121
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:51,120
Hawxing,

122
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,780
when you defeat the one who has never understood

123
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:54,600
what it means to love and be loved—the Illumin-Eye,

124
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,100
you’ll gain nothing.

125
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,720
Whatever the outcome.

126
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:01,060
I'll verify it in my own way.

127
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,379
Just as I expected.

128
00:09:07,379 --> 00:09:09,220
So even this can't stop you...?

129
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:23,820
The eyes of tomorrow are sparkling,

130
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:27,180
a smile that faces the sun.

131
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:31,780
Bravely speak what your heart holds dear—

132
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,780
that little spark of emotion.

133
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:39,200
A morning breeze blows in,

134
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,520
carrying away the wish of all these years.

135
00:10:42,519 --> 00:10:47,759
It will quietly plant it at the crossroads up ahead.

136
00:10:47,759 --> 00:10:55,480
It will quietly plant it at the crossroads up ahead.